  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\n\nClosed upper low will move away from CWA tonight with SW upper\nflow to replace it Tuesday. Monsoonal moisture will stay south of\nthe CWA Tuesday but higher clouds will increase.\n\nThe southwest flow will increase Wednesday with an upper trough\ndigging over the Pacific NW. Scattered showers will increase in\ncoverage as they move into the northern zones during the evening.\n\nWith the southwest flow this week, temperatures will warm into \nthe 80s most places with Friday looking to be the warmest day.\nTemps reaching 90 is possible over the southeast zones.\n\nLater this week, the upper trough becomes an upper low and could\nbring another round of showers into the area late in the weekend\nor early next week.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nNBM was mainly followed through this period. TFJ",
